sequenceDiagram
    participant GH as GitHub Actions CI
    participant UT as pytest tests/unit/
    participant DL as download_financebench.py
    participant CI as run_ci_eval.py
    participant PL as Full Pipeline (search_filings)
    participant RA as ragas.evaluate()
    participant NA as numerical_accuracy()
    participant GS as GitHub PR Comment

    GH->>UT: pytest tests/unit/ -v
    UT-->>GH: all unit tests pass (260 as of 2026-09-28, grows over time)

    GH->>DL: python scripts/download_financebench.py
    DL->>DL: fetch PatronusAI/financebench JSONL from HuggingFace<br/>(financebench_merged.jsonl, not GitHub/CSV), take first 150 rows
    DL-->>GH: evals/eval_data/financebench_150.json

    GH->>CI: python evals/run_ci_eval.py
    loop For each of 30 questions
        CI->>PL: build_search_filings_answer(question)
        PL->>PL: rewrite → hybrid BM25+Pinecone → rerank → generate → verify
        PL-->>CI: {answer, citations, cost_usd, latency_ms}
    end

    CI->>RA: score_dataset(questions, answers, contexts, ground_truths)
    RA->>RA: faithfulness (LLM-as-judge: is answer supported by context?)
    RA->>RA: answer_relevancy (LLM: does answer address the question?)
    RA->>RA: context_precision (LLM: are retrieved chunks relevant?)
    RA->>RA: context_recall (LLM: did retrieval capture all needed info?)
    RA-->>CI: {faithfulness, answer_relevancy, context_precision, context_recall}

    CI->>NA: numerical_accuracy(answers, contexts)
    NA->>NA: extract all numbers from answers (regex)
    NA->>NA: normalise formats ($26.4B == 26400000000.0)
    NA->>NA: check each number appears in source chunks
    NA-->>CI: score 0.0-1.0

    CI->>CI: write evals/results/ci_latest.json
    CI->>CI: assert faithfulness >= 0.85
    CI->>CI: assert numerical_accuracy >= 0.90
    CI-->>GH: pass / fail

    GH->>GS: post scores table as PR comment

    Note over RA: ragas judges with OpenAI gpt-4o-mini, not Bedrock --<br/>deliberate: Bedrock's rate limits throttle 4 LLM calls per<br/>question x 30 questions, gpt-4o-mini doesn't (ragas_metrics.py)
    Note over NA: custom metric -- ragas has no financial number grounding check
    Note over CI: 30 questions = fast CI gate. The planned weekly full-eval<br/>workflow (nightly_eval.yml) does not exist yet -- evals/run_eval.py<br/>is run manually (see CLAUDE.md "Known gaps")
